-- DICT-SEMANTICS §8 I7 qualification 4 (issue 1539) -- THE GATE, class `Num`.
--
-- EXPECTED VALUE HAND-DERIVED FROM THE SPEC, NOT CAPTURED. I7: "the class its
-- synthesized predicate names is a fixed constant of the language, denoting the
-- PRELUDE's declaration of that class". Qualification 4: absent the prelude the
-- predicate is "not merely undischarged -- not synthesized", and the gate that decides
-- that MUST be "is the PRELUDE's class present". This program HAS the prelude, so the
-- `Num Blob` predicate IS synthesized; `Blob` has no `impl Num`, so §3 cannot discharge
-- it and the program is REJECTED, `T-NO-IMPL`. That derivation fixes the verdict before
-- any binary was run.
--
-- WHY THIS FIXTURE CAN FAIL, which is the only reason to add it (#1554): the gate is
-- the ONLY thing standing between this file and exit 0. Switch `builtinClassPresent
-- BNum` off and no obligation is recorded, `check` ACCEPTS, and the row flips
-- REJECT->ACCEPT. Measured, not assumed: a stubbed `builtinClassPresent _ = False`
-- build accepts this file at exit 0.
--
-- ⚠️ SHAPE NOTES, each of which is load-bearing and was arrived at by a failed draft:
--   * the operator's operands are a SIGNATURE-typed parameter, never a numeric literal.
--     `Blob 1 + Blob 2` instead reports `Type mismatch: Int literal vs Blob` from the
--     numlit-taint reframe -- a diagnostic the unify raises whether or not the gate
--     fired, so that shape cannot discriminate the gate at all.
--   * `main` does not `println` a `Blob`, which would add an unrelated `No impl of
--     Display for Blob` and let the row pass on the wrong diagnostic.
--   * `main = println 1` keeps a numeric literal in the file on purpose: it is the
--     `inferNumLit` gate's own path, and it must stay ACCEPTED.
--
-- ⚠️ These four sibling fixtures (num/eq/ord/semigroup) discriminate a PER-CLASS gate
-- that has gone off. They do NOT discriminate a swapped presence FIELD (bcOrdPresent
-- read where bcEqPresent was meant): in any prelude-loaded program all four bits are
-- True together, so a swap is unobservable here by construction. Nothing in this tree
-- can see that swap while the prelude is the only source of the four classes.
data Blob = Blob Int

twice : Blob -> Blob
twice x = x + x

main = println 1
